{
 "about": "What a request from the dedicated tab carries (appendix A 13, 29 and the planning session's measurement of the app's own requests on 2026-10-18). headers: each header the app sends and where its value comes from in the logged-in tab; method: when the app uses POST; read_only: which operations may ever be sent; features: how the features parameter is filled; variables: what each surface sends (the previous skill's registry, to be checked against the app's own requests in P2 R7/R8). All values are synthetic; no real bearer, token or query id appears here.",
 "headers": {
  "item": "13",
  "source": "measured",
  "fact": "The app's GraphQL requests are XHR to https://x.com/i/api/graphql/<queryId>/<operationName> with exactly these headers; a request is not sent when any source is missing (no bearer in the modules, no ct0 cookie, no signature generator).",
  "set": {
   "authorization": "Bearer <the bearer string found in the app's modules>",
   "x-twitter-auth-type": "OAuth2Session",
   "x-csrf-token": "<the ct0 cookie>",
   "x-twitter-client-language": "<the store's session.language>",
   "x-twitter-active-user": "yes",
   "content-type": "application/json",
   "x-client-transaction-id": "<the app's own generator called with (host, path without query or fragment, method)>"
  },
  "polling_only": {
   "x-twitter-polling": "true"
  },
  "never": [
   "origin",
   "referer",
   "user-agent",
   "cookie"
  ],
  "missing_cases": [
   {
    "missing": "bearer",
    "expected": {
     "sent": false,
     "reason": "missing"
    }
   },
   {
    "missing": "ct0",
    "expected": {
     "sent": false,
     "reason": "login"
    }
   },
   {
    "missing": "generator",
    "expected": {
     "sent": false,
     "reason": "missing"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
 "method": {
  "item": "29",
  "source": "measured (the app client's module source)",
  "fact": "The app sends POST only for a mutation or when its caller passes forcePost; every query the skill sends is GET with variables, features and fieldToggles as JSON in the query string. The previous skill sent the home feeds as POST (it imitated a request that carried the ids the app had already seen); the skill sends them as GET.",
  "cases": [
