 "features": {
  "item": "7,plan",
  "source": "measured (featureSwitches from modules, values from the store) + plan, P2 R7 (fieldToggles values)",
  "fact": "features is every name in the operation's featureSwitches list (from its module definition), each with the store's value (featureSwitch.user.config[name].value); a name the store does not know is false. fieldToggles is the operation's fieldToggles list; its values are not in the store — the previous registry sent withArticleRichContentState, withArticleSummaryText and withArticleVoiceOver true on TweetDetail, and P2 R7 decides the values from the app's own requests. When X answers 'features cannot be null: a, b', those names are added the same way and the request is retried once.",
